This means that the Tribunal should consider and decide with reference to the evidence:
28. (i) whether the disablement is permanent or temporary;
(ii) if the disablement is permanent, whether it is permanent total disablement or permanent partial disablement;
(iii) if the disablement percentage is expressed with MACT No. 726/19 Akshay Pokhriyal v. Pappu Pal Page No. 9 of 23 BK reference to any specific limb, then the effect of such disablement of the limb on the functioning of the entire body,that is, the permanent disability suffered by the person.
